  "traps": ["DSColors.readable(_:) and DSColors.secondaryText resolve a color with the high-contrast trait on iOS, but AppKit has no equivalent: NSAppearance(named:) returns nil for the high-contrast names (NSAppearance.h, macOS 27 SDK), so on the Mac they blend the color toward black or white until it reaches 4.5 to 1 against the window background (Theme.swift, legible). A Mac change that skips that path draws plain systemGray at about 3.4 to 1 (2026-10-16).", "Words on a tinted chip or pill are in the label color, with the color kept in the icon and the tint: colored words on a pale tint of themselves measured 3.5 to 4.1 to 1 even in Apple's high-contrast colors (2026-10-16, Docs/ai/DECISIONS.md)."]
